<item><title>Sierra Leone charcoal trade sustains burners as tree loss threatens food security</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-burners-as-tree-loss-a237a3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-burners-as-tree-loss-a237a3/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A government energy compact says 36% of people have electricity access and only 15% have access to clean cooking.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:55:17 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-burners-as-tree-loss-a237a3/share.jpg" length="43035" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-burners-as-tree-loss-a237a3/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Sierra Leone finance minister faces civil-society call for dismissal</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-finance-minister-faces-civil-society-call-for-c955ed/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-finance-minister-faces-civil-society-call-for-c955ed/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>The CSOs Consortium on Public Accountability says Sheku Bangura should be removed, while a guest writer defends his record on inflation and debt.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:55:17 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-finance-minister-faces-civil-society-call-for-c955ed/share.jpg" length="42611" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-finance-minister-faces-civil-society-call-for-c955ed/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Analyst asks whether Sierra Leone&apos;s vice presidency is a dead end</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/analyst-asks-whether-sierra-leone-s-vice-presidency-is-a-b42fab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/analyst-asks-whether-sierra-leone-s-vice-presidency-is-a-b42fab/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>Foday M. Daboh, a public policy analyst, argues that vice presidents have rarely been groomed as successors and often enter office without an independent political base.</description><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:55:17 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
